IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art13-effects`
IMPORT `g5-art13-reporting`
IMPORT `g5-art14-court-powers`
IMPORT `g5-tests-fixtures`

-- g5-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT TO FAIL, and are counted: 16 failed assertions, no other error, no refusal and no warning.
-- Each one states, of a discriminating case of the fork register, the answer that the OTHER reading gives, and asks it of the reading taken.
-- It therefore fails exactly because the two readings differ on that case; the file is also the proof that the harness can fail.
-- (A reading is taken in `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`; the other readings are the `the interpretation with ...` values.)

§ `Assertions of the other readings, asked of the reading taken (expected: 16 failures)`

`the favoured reading` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`

§§ `F5.1 and F5.10: promptly`

`the March matter` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 3 20

`a report on 25 March 2026, judged not prompt` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 25)
    `the report was made promptly` IS FALSE

-- Reading C (14 days from awareness) answers TRUE; the reading taken takes the input judgement (not prompt) and answers FALSE.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (1).
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` `the favoured reading` `the March matter` `a report on 25 March 2026, judged not prompt`
-- Reading B of F5.10 puts the last prompt day at 14 March; the reading taken puts it at 15 March.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (2).
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the last prompt day` `the favoured reading` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14

§§ `F5.2 and F5.11: the year of the return`

`a day in the autumn of 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 12 1

-- Reading B (financial year ending 30 June) gives 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027; the reading taken gives the calendar year.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (3).
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 7 1), (YMD 2027 6 30)
-- Reading C (from the anniversary of registration, 1 March 2019) gives 1 March 2026 to 28 February 2027.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (4).
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026` EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2027 2 28)

-- A registration on 29 February 2020, reference day 28 February 2025: the year began on 28 February 2025 on the reading taken (clamped); rolled to 1 March, it
-- began on 29 February 2024.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (5).
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the leap day charity` NOTHING (YMD 2025 2 28) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2024 2 29), (YMD 2025 2 28)

§§ `F5.3: an Order under paragraph (8)`

-- On the literal reading no Order exists under (8), so a relief Order naming one reaches nothing; on the reading taken it reaches the provisions made by virtue of (8).  EXPECTED TO FAIL (6).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the relief Order names the provision` `the favoured reading` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`

§§ `F5.4: misconduct in the administration of the charity`

`a conviction with no bearing on the administration` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

`mismanagement that breaks no provision` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS TRUE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS TRUE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- Reading B (any misconduct within Article 2(10)) answers TRUE for a conviction with no bearing on the administration.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (7).
#ASSERT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the favoured reading` TRUE `a conviction with no bearing on the administration`
-- Reading C (the ordinary sense) answers TRUE for mismanagement that is not misconduct within Article 2(10).  EXPECTED TO FAIL (8).
#ASSERT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the favoured reading` FALSE `mismanagement that breaks no provision`

§§ `F5.5: a return sent on the due date`

`an Order due on 31 March 2027` MEANS `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` WITH
    `due date of the annual return` IS JUST (YMD 2027 3 31)
    `consequence of lateness` IS NOTHING

-- Reading B (must be sent before the due date) calls a return sent on the due date late.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (9).
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the favoured reading` `an Order due on 31 March 2027` (YMD 2027 3 31)

§§ `F5.6: the day deregistration takes effect`

-- Reading B (the effective day is still a day of registration).  EXPECTED TO FAIL (10).
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` (YMD 2022 6 30)

§§ `F5.7: a purpose that is not charitable`

-- Reading B does not catch a purely ancillary purpose.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (11).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` (YMD 2023 1 1) `a provision permitting a purely ancillary purpose`

§§ `F5.8: paragraphs (a) and (b) of Article 13(5)`

-- Reading B: once a prior permission is given the different condition replaces the original, so a charity that fails the different condition does not comply.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (12).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity with a prior permission that still meets its original condition and fails the different one`

§§ `F5.9: the first day of a period fixed by the court`

`a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` MEANS `a specified period` (YMD 2026 6 1) 30

-- Reading B starts the period on 2 June, so 1 June is not in it.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (13).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 6 1)

§§ `F5.12: the purposes of an order under Article 14(2)`

`an order only to protect the property` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS FALSE, `to protect the property` IS TRUE, `to secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- Reading B (all three purposes) refuses an order that only protects the property.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (14).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order only to protect the property`

§§ `F5.13: when a matter arises`

`an event of 30 December 2026 that the charity learned of on 5 January 2027` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 12 30
    `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2027 1 5

`the calendar year 2026` MEANS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)

-- Reading B (the day the charity became aware) puts the matter in 2027, outside the 2026 return.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (15).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` `an event of 30 December 2026 that the charity learned of on 5 January 2027`

§§ `F5.14: which statement a payment is judged by`

-- Reading B ("a statement provided" includes the first one) calls the payment inconsistent although the amended statement in force allows it.  EXPECTED TO FAIL (16).
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment that fits the amended statement but not the first`

